From 92917b6ff96cbdbd803d8015100c7f02ed365087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:10:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] plugin_api: let a desktop plugin use Files and the
 keyboard over its desktop

A Host API 2 worker that opened the optional desktop could not ask for a
file while the desktop was up (PICK_FILE was refused), could not show or
hide AERA's on-screen keyboard for a focused text field, never learned
how much of its frame the keyboard covered, and lost every key that has
no ASCII keysym.

Add kFeatureDesktopIntegration (bit 12), negotiated like the other
optional features through the HELLO request marker:

- PICK_FILE is accepted while the desktop is open. The Files selection
  opens over it and suspends desktop input for as long as it is open:
  held keys get their key-up, RELEASE is sent, a shown keyboard is
  hidden, and touches, mouse and keys go to Files. A press that began on
  the guest is swallowed until it is released; one that began on Files
  ends there. Every close path (select, cancel, a new page, leaving the
  view, the worker stopping) restores input and a requested keyboard.
- SET_DESKTOP_KEYBOARD (worker kind 29) shows or hides the keyboard,
  with the number or multiline layout. Contacts above the shown keyboard
  still reach the guest; Done sends Return.
- DESKTOP_KEYBOARD_INSET (host kind 76) reports the framebuffer rows the
  keyboard covers: 0 after DESKTOP_READY, then on each show and hide,
  including the toolbar's KEYS button, which now toggles.
- On-screen keys without an ASCII keysym are sent as X11 keysyms (the
  Latin-1 code point, else 0x01000000 | code point).

The new kinds are valid only after the bit was acknowledged: the session
closes a worker that sends one unnegotiated and never sends one to it.
Workers that do not request the bit keep the previous behaviour, values
and ACK flags exactly.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
