+### Desktop integration (optional)
+
+Request `kFeatureDesktopIntegration` (bit 12) together with `kFeatureDesktop`
+and check the ACK. Without it the desktop behaves exactly as above: Files
+cannot open over it, its keyboard sends ASCII keysyms only, and no keyboard
+geometry is reported. The kinds below are valid only after the
+bit was acknowledged; an unacknowledged one closes the session.
+
+- `PICK_FILE` is also accepted while the desktop is open. The regular Files
+  selection opens over it. While it is open, desktop input is suspended: AERA
+  sends key-ups for held physical keys and `RELEASE`, hides a shown desktop
+  keyboard, and gives touches, mouse and keys to Files. A press that began on
+  the guest is swallowed until released; one that began on Files ends there.
+  Selecting, cancelling, a new page, leaving the view or stopping the worker
+  closes Files and restores input and a keyboard the worker had requested.
+  Only single file or folder selection exists; there is no multiple selection
+  or save dialog.
+- `SET_DESKTOP_KEYBOARD` (worker kind 29): nonzero `request_id`, `value` 0
+  hides and 1 shows AERA's on-screen keyboard over the desktop, `flags` is 0,
+  `kInputNumber` (2) or `kInputMultiline` (4) (not both), empty strings. A
+  request while no desktop is open is ignored. The multiline layout replaces
+  Done with Return; Done in the other layouts sends Return and hides the
+  keyboard. A contact that starts above the keyboard still reaches the guest.
+  The toolbar `KEYS` button toggles the text keyboard.
+- `DESKTOP_KEYBOARD_INSET` (host kind 76): `request_id` 0, `value` the rows
+  of the desktop framebuffer (in its negotiated height) that the keyboard
+  covers from the bottom, `flags` 0. The host sends 0 right after
+  `DESKTOP_READY` and then on every show or hide, including the user's Done,
+  the toolbar and a suspension by Files.
+- On-screen keys without an ASCII keysym are sent as X11 keysyms: Latin-1
+  characters as their code point (`é` is `0xe9`), others as
+  `0x01000000 | code point` (`€` is `0x010020ac`). ASCII keys are unchanged.
+
 ## Optional background, activities and presentation
 
 These extensions keep protocol version 2 and the same packet size. A new worker
